# G15 driver review
results/WAVE3/G15/close_march.py is a byte-identical copy of results/WAVE2/F2/close_march.py
(cmp: identical). Diff against results/WAVE1/W19/scripts/close_march.py follows below.

Checked:
(a) fresh directory per job: march() uses tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="m_<tag>_", dir=WORK) and solve()
    uses tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="s_<k>_", dir=WORK) for every CaDiCaL + cake_lpr job; the CNF,
    LRAT proof and solver output live only there, and the directory is removed afterwards.
    No shared s_k names (AUDIT RISK-3(b)). WORK=/opt/work/tmp on this VM.
(b) atomic outputs: finalize() writes leaves.icnf and open.icnf with tempfile.mkstemp in OUTDIR and
    os.replace() into place, every line "a ... 0\n" (AUDIT RISK-1).
(c) the first leaves.jsonl record is {"case": <--name>, "case_sha256": sha256 of the case CNF},
    written only when leaves.jsonl does not yet exist; run with --name U_L7. A second "top"
    record carries top_sha256 and case_sha256.
Also: a leaf enters leaves.icnf only when status == "UNSAT" and cake_lpr == "s VERIFIED UNSAT"
exactly (AUDIT BUG-1; also RISK-3(a)); other verdicts become UNSAT_UNCHECKED and stay open.
--skip (F2 step d) is not used here, so no SKIP records arise.
Known liveness limits (AUDIT NOTE-1, no false claims): a march refutation writing "a 0" would make
a child equal to its parent; worker exceptions are swallowed (the cube then stays open/uncovered).
Leaves are full cubes over F's variables (top cube + split sub-cube literals); the case units
come from the case CNF.

